insert into public.dsa_problems (id,topic_id,title,difficulty,slug,description,examples,test_cases,constraints,hints,starter_code,editorial,solution_code,solution_approach,supported_languages,sql_schema_sql,sql_seed_sql,learning_topic_id,status,is_premium,show_on_website,show_on_mobile,sort_order) select 'cx-department-headcount-view',null::text,'Create department headcounts','Easy','department-headcount-view','Create a view named department_counts exposing department and headcount for every department represented in employees. The checker reads it ordered by department.

**MySQL dialect.**

```sql
CREATE TABLE employees(id INT PRIMARY KEY,department VARCHAR(30) NOT NULL);
INSERT INTO employees VALUES(1,''Arts''),(2,''Arts''),(3,''Science'');
```

**Required ordering:** Checker orders department ascending.

**Edge cases:**
- One employee department.
