insert into public.dsa_problems (id,topic_id,title,difficulty,slug,description,examples,test_cases,constraints,hints,starter_code,editorial,solution_code,solution_approach,supported_languages,sql_schema_sql,sql_seed_sql,learning_topic_id,status,is_premium,show_on_website,show_on_mobile,sort_order) select 'cp-dbms-sql-orders-placed-in-march-2026',null::text,'Orders Placed in March 2026','Medium','orders-placed-in-march-2026','Write a query returning `id`, `customer_name`, `order_date` for every order placed in March 2026 (the 1st through the 31st, inclusive), ordered by `id`. (This case may legitimately return zero rows if no order falls in that month.)

**MySQL dialect.**

```sql
CREATE TABLE orders (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  customer_name TEXT NOT NULL,
  amount INTEGER NOT NULL,
  order_date DATE NOT NULL
);
INSERT INTO orders (id, customer_name, amount, order_date) VALUES
(1, ''Asha'', 500, ''2026-03-05''),
(2, ''Rohan'', 300, ''2026-03-20''),
(3, ''Neha'', 700, ''2026-04-02''),
(4, ''Asha'', 200, ''2026-03-28'');
```

**Required ordering:** Retain the ordering stated in the original task.

**Edge cases:**
