**MySQL dialect.**

```sql
CREATE TABLE products (
  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
  name TEXT NOT NULL,
  category TEXT NOT NULL,
  price INTEGER NOT NULL,
  stock INTEGER
);
INSERT INTO products (id, name, category, price, stock) VALUES
(1, ''ProLaptop'', ''Electronics'', 85000, 12),
(2, ''Notebook'', ''Stationery'', 40, NULL),
(3, ''Python Basics'', ''Books'', 350, 5),
(4, ''ProPhone'', ''Electronics'', 45000, 0),
(5, ''Novel'', ''Books'', 220, NULL),
(6, ''Desk Lamp'', ''Home'', 900, 8);
```

**Required ordering:** As explicitly ordered in the result query.

**Edge cases:**
- Pro itself qualifies.
- A name containing Pro only later is excluded.','[{"input": "INSERT INTO products (id, name, category, price, stock) VALUES\n(1, ''ProLaptop'', ''Electronics'', 85000, 12),\n(2, ''Notebook'', ''Stationery'', 40, NULL),\n(3, ''Python Basics'', ''Books'', 350, 5),\n(4, ''ProPhone'', ''Electronics'', 45000, 0),\n(5, ''Novel'', ''Books'', 220, NULL),\n(6, ''Desk Lamp'', ''Home'', 900, 8);", "output": "id\tname\n1\tProLaptop\n4\tProPhone", "explanation": "The fixed prefix and trailing wildcard match the retained catalogue names. Percent accepts an empty suffix; a later occurrence of Pro is not enough. This retained schema does not declare a universal case-sensitive collation.", "check_sql": ""}]'::jsonb,'[{"seed_sql": "INSERT INTO products (id, name, category, price, stock) VALUES\n(1, ''ProTablet'', ''Electronics'', 32000, 4),\n(2, ''Pencil Set'', ''Stationery'', 60, NULL),\n(3, ''SQL Guide'', ''Books'', 500, 10),\n(4, ''ProSpeaker'', ''Electronics'', 6000, 0);", "expected": "id\tname\n1\tProTablet\n4\tProSpeaker", "hidden": true}, {"seed_sql": "INSERT INTO products VALUES (1,''Pro'',''Electronics'',1,1),(2,''XPro'',''Books'',1,1);", "expected": "id\tname\n1\tPro", "hidden": true}, {"seed_sql": "INSERT INTO products VALUES (1,''Notebook'',''Books'',1,1);", "expected": "", "hidden": true}]'::jsonb,'["Use only the supplied synthetic tables and requested transition.", "Preserve unrelated rows."]'::jsonb,'["Place percent after the fixed prefix.", "Keep the original output id ordering."]'::jsonb,'{"sql": "-- Write your SELECT query here\n"}'::jsonb,'The fixed prefix and trailing wildcard match the retained catalogue names. Percent accepts an empty suffix; a later occurrence of Pro is not enough. This retained schema does not declare a universal case-sensitive collation.','{"sql": "SELECT id,name FROM products WHERE name LIKE ''Pro%'' ORDER BY id;"}'::jsonb,'The fixed prefix and trailing wildcard match the retained catalogue names. Percent accepts an empty suffix; a later occurrence of Pro is not enough. This retained schema does not declare a universal case-sensitive collation.',array['sql'],'CREATE TABLE products (
