**MySQL dialect.**

```sql
CREATE TABLE departments (department_id INT PRIMARY KEY,department_name VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL); CREATE TABLE employees (employee_id INT PRIMARY KEY,employee_name VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL,department_id INT NOT NULL);
INSERT INTO departments VALUES (10,''Engineering''),(20,''Sales''),(30,''Research''); INSERT INTO employees VALUES (1,''Asha'',10),(2,''Rohan'',10),(3,''Neha'',20);
```

**Required ordering:** Order rows by the key specified in the task.

**Edge cases:**
- Empty input returns no detail rows.
- Include equal values on different source rows.
- Verify boundary and NULL handling when the schema permits them.','[{"input": "INSERT INTO departments VALUES (10,''Engineering''),(20,''Sales''),(30,''Research''); INSERT INTO employees VALUES (1,''Asha'',10),(2,''Rohan'',10),(3,''Neha'',20);", "output": "employee_id\temployee_name\tdepartment_name\n1\tAsha\tEngineering\n2\tRohan\tEngineering\n3\tNeha\tSales", "explanation": "The solution implements the stated row selection and preserves the requested result grain; the final ordering makes comparisons deterministic."}]'::jsonb,'[{"seed_sql": "INSERT INTO departments VALUES (5,''Services''),(6,''Services''); INSERT INTO employees VALUES (2,''B'',6),(1,''A'',5);", "expected": "employee_id\temployee_name\tdepartment_name\n1\tA\tServices\n2\tB\tServices", "hidden": true}]'::jsonb,'[]'::jsonb,'["Determine the result grain before writing the query.", "Use explicit projected columns and a final ORDER BY."]'::jsonb,'{"sql": "-- Write your SELECT query here\n"}'::jsonb,'The solution implements the stated row selection and preserves the requested result grain; the final ordering makes comparisons deterministic.','{"sql": "SELECT e.employee_id,e.employee_name,d.department_name FROM employees e JOIN departments d ON d.department_id=e.department_id ORDER BY e.employee_id;"}'::jsonb,'The solution implements the stated row selection and preserves the requested result grain; the final ordering makes comparisons deterministic.',array['sql'],'CREATE TABLE departments (department_id INT PRIMARY KEY,department_name VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL); CREATE TABLE employees (employee_id INT PRIMARY KEY,employee_name VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL,department_id INT NOT NULL);','INSERT INTO departments VALUES (10,''Engineering''),(20,''Sales''),(30,''Research''); INSERT INTO employees VALUES (1,''Asha'',10),(2,''Rohan'',10),(3,''Neha'',20);',topic_uuid,parent.status,parent.is_premium,parent.show_on_website,parent.show_on_mobile,1 from public.practice_tests parent where parent.id='pt-dbms-sql-21-transitive-dep